Release notes, 6 August 2026

Version 0.3.0 went out across every registry. This was the first release where all of them carry the same version at the same time.

The npm packages, the Python package and the Rust crate all published from a single tag. The Go module picks up tags automatically and needs nothing. The VS Code extension versions independently and went to 0.4.1.

Crates.io published for the first time ever. The registry token had never been configured, so the release workflow had been skipping that job with a warning rather than failing, which meant the crate silently did not exist through several releases. Subbu created the token and reran just that job.

A lesson from the previous release: the tag drives every registry in lockstep, so leaving Python at an older version would have made the publish job fail on a duplicate version. All SDK versions now move together even when a language has no code change that cycle.

Verification was done against the registry APIs rather than the workflow status. That caught PyPI reporting an old version from cache while the release was actually present, which reading the job status alone would have missed in one direction and reading the cached field alone would have missed in the other.

Maven Central is still manual. It needs a GPG key and namespace verification that cannot be scripted.

